    "eligibility": "The Bharti Airtel Scholarship Program, an initiative of the Bharti Airtel Foundation, aims to support deserving students from diverse socio-economic backgrounds, with a particular focus on girls, in their pursuit of becoming future technology leaders. This merit-cum-means-based scholarship program has been designed for deserving students enrolled in technology-based engineering undergraduate and 5 year integrated courses in the top 50 NIRF-ranked (Engineering) universities/institutes as per the latest NIRF ranking. The students receiving the scholarship shall be called Bharti Scholars.\nThis fully funded scholarship aims to remove financial barriers that prevent deserving students from accessing quality education. It covers 100% annual fees, including meal and accommodation charges. Additionally, all Bharti Scholars are provided a laptop in their first year to aid in their academic journey.\n\nEligibility\n• Confirmed admission or enrollment in the first year (academic year 2025-2026) of the undergraduate/5 year integrated courses in fields of Electronics & Communication, Telecom, Information Technology, Computer Sciences, Data Sciences, Aerospace and Emerging Technologies (AI, IoT, AR/VR, Machine Learning, Robotics) at the top 50 NIRF ranked Engineering universities/institutes. (Basis the 2024 list available).\n• Must be a citizen and resident of India.\n• Parents’/guardians’ annual income from all sources should not exceed INR 8.5 lakhs.\n• Preference shall be given to students who are girls, persons with disabilities, have single /no parents and transgender.\n• Applicants should not be recipients of any other scholarships/ grants for the same purposes as being supported by the Bharti Airtel Foundation.\n\nDocuments• Proof of identity (Aadhaar card)\n• Current year admission proof (admission letter, fees letter from the university/institution)\n• The marksheet of Class 12\n• JEE scorecard or university entrance exam scorecard (whichever applicable)\n• Parental/Guardian income documents:\n• If salaried/self-employed- latest Income Tax Returns Form (complete form) and bank statement of the previous 6 months. Income tax acknowledgement receipts will not be considered as valid income proof.\n• If no taxable income/unemployed - Government-issued income certificate and bank statement of previous 6 months.\n• Bank account details (such as account number, IFSC, branch address) and bank statement of the applicant and parent/guardian of the last 6 months\n• Bank account details of the institution (such as name of account, account number, IFSC, branch address)\n• A recent passport-sized photograph of the applicant\n• Documents about extra-curricular activities, achievements, part-time jobs, projects, innovations, etc.\n• Expense receipts/rent agreement (in case staying in PG/rented accommodation), if applicable\n• Statement of purpose (SOP) from the applicant",
