    "full_website": "https://www.imsc.res.in/~nbhm/",
    "eligibility": "The National Board for Higher Mathematics (NBHM), Government of India, provides scholarships to encourage talented students to pursue higher studies and research in Mathematics and Statistics.\n\n1. NBHM Masters Scholarship\n\n• The scholarship is offered to outstanding students pursuing Master's degree programmes in Mathematics or Statistics, with an aptitude for higher studies and research.\n\nSelection: Selection is based on a written test and interview conducted as prescribed by NBHM.\n\nStudents can avail the NBHM M.Sc. fellowship only once under the scheme.\n\n2. NBHM Doctoral Scholarship\n\n• The NBHM Doctoral Scholarship is intended for students pursuing doctoral research in Mathematics\n\nEligibility: Candidates possessing a Master's degree in Mathematics, or Statistics and wishing to pursue research leading to a Ph.D. in any branch of Mathematics can apply.\n\n• The scholarship can be held for up to five years, subject to the prescribed conditions and satisfactory progress.\n\nSelection Process\n\nSelection for the Ph.D. scholarship is based on the result of a Selection Test and Interview conducted by a committee constituted by NBHM.\n\nApplication & Updates\n\nStudents should check the official NBHM website for the latest notification, eligibility conditions, application dates and application procedure.",
