    "eligibility": "PM Foundation Centers of Excellence Scholarships are provided to students studying in reputed institutions that are selected by the Foundation as Centres of Excellence. It was started in the year 2013 with the objective of supporting financially backward students who are enrolled in the reputed institutions for their higher studies. Even though the Fees in these institutes are low, the students find it difficult to afford the hostel and other living expenses. So, PM Foundation support the students for the same. Till date, PM Foundation have supported 430 students.\n\nProcedure\n• Applications are invited in the month of Aug/Sep, every year\n• Candidates are requested to submit all the required documents\n• Interview will be held for the shortlisted students\nEligibility Criteria\nStudents who are pursuing UG/PG courses in the following institutions selected by the P M Foundation as CENTRES OF EXCELLENCE (listed below) can apply for the scholarship\n\n• A J K Mass Communication Research Centre (AJK MCRC), Delhi\n• All India Institute of Medical Science (AIIMS)\n• Asian School of Journalism, Chennai\n• Bhabha Atomic Research Centre (BARC), Mumbai\n• Center for Development Studies, CDS- TVM\n• Delhi School of Economics- Delhi\n• Faculty of Management studies, Delhi\n• I I M\n• I I T\n• Indian Agricultural Research Institute (IARI) – PUSA, Delhi\n• Indian Institute of Mass Communication (IIMC)\n• Indian Institute of Science (IISc), Bengaluru\n• Indian Institute of Science Education and Research( IISER)\n• Indian Statistical Institute (ISI) Kolkata\n• Indira Gandhi Institute of Development Research (IGIDR), Mumbai\n• Institute of Rural Management Anand, Gujarat (IRMA)\n• J N U, New Delhi\n• Jawaharlal Institute of Postgraduate Medical Education & Research, Pudussery\n• Lady Sriram College for women, New Delhi\n• Loyola College, Chennai\n• M.S University Baroda (for Fine Arts)\n• Madras Christian College, Chennai\n• Miranda House, New Delhi\n• National Institute of Design, Ahmedabad\n• National Law School of India, Bengaluru\n• Saha Institute of Nuclear Physics, Kolkotta\n• School of planning and architecture, Delhi\n• Sriram College of Commerce, New Delhi\n• St. Stephen’s College, New Delhi\n• Tata Institute of Fundamental Research (TIFR), Mumbai\n• Tata Institute of Social Sciences (T I S S), Mumbai\n• Teri University, New Delhi\n• Xavier Labour Relations Institute (XLRI), Jamshedpur",
